  "rationale": "R9 (#804) — the declared-type reference graph, a family standard the csharp lane was missing entirely (rust's R13 header: \"family standard, mirrors go/c/zig\"; ten lanes implement it, measured by script/m60/declared-type-refs-census.ts). This fixture pins every position that WRITES a type name (field / variable declaration, parameter, return type, property, indexer, event, delegate), every shape a written type can take (bare, array, nullable, qualified, generic base AND argument, tuple, pointer, ref), the source-attribution contract measured off java/kotlin/python (a member's dependency belongs to the enclosing TYPE, a parameter's / return's / local's to the enclosing CALLABLE), the two markers (declared_type, and return_type for returns — java/kotlin/python/typescript all use return_type), and the four ways this walk can publish a NAME that is not a type: a tuple element's name, a bound type parameter, a predefined type, and `var`. Measured 2026-09-22 before the pins were written; the tuple-element and bound-parameter defects below were FOUND BY THIS FIXTURE'S OWN FIRST MEASUREMENT.",
